# Agentic Testability Gate

Use this skill to prevent optimistic validation. The agent must identify what
must be testable, run the right level of evidence, and state residual risk before
claiming code is ready.

This skill complements `agentic-code-review`: code review can find implementation
risks, but this gate decides whether the changed behavior was proven at the
right level of the stack.

## Load Order

Read only what applies:

1. Start here for every activation.
2. Use `references/obligation-matrix.md` for the required evidence schema and
   final result format.
3. Use `references/test-quality-calibration.md` when choosing unit,
   integration, contract, E2E, coverage, flake, mutation, or regression tests.
4. Use `references/browser-visual-evidence.md` for UI, browser, visual,
   accessibility, responsive, branding, tenant, or personalization changes.
5. Use `references/ci-monorepo-gates.md` for monorepos, microservices, CI,
   affected graph, service-suite, and pipeline hardening decisions.
6. Use `references/agentic-code-review-integration.md` when this gate is part of
   an implementation closeout or review approval.
7. Use `references/pressure-tests.md` to audit whether the skill is being
